  "description": "The session record at contract-v0.3, additive on v0.2 (immortality §6.4): every v0.2 record stays valid. It gains the attached clients (clients: client_id, user, may_control — may_control when the client's principal holds session.join.rw), whether the target is resizable and whether it is pinned (terminal-size-and-control.md §3; 5.50). All three are optional in the schema so a v0.2 core's record stays valid; a v0.3 core puts them on every record not ended. The v0.2 invalid cases — an ended session with a countdown, half a countdown, unreachable without a reason, an unreachable_reason on a reachable record, a lifetime cap, the worker's own state — are unchanged. The live run of session-countdown validates real records against the same shape.",
  "corpus": [
    "terminal-size-and-control.md §3",
    "C1 decision 1",
    "C2 decision 5",
    "C2 decision 8",
    "immortality §6.4"
  ],
